# Goal: start N-sample calibration collection (see
# CalibrationBroadcasterConfig::num_samples for the default N — this is
# empty for now since overriding N per-call isn't needed yet, matching the
# project's convention of tuning via YAML params, not per-call args).
---
# Result: final status once collection finishes (success) or is aborted.
# The computed transform itself is not duplicated here — it's already
# broadcast on /tf by calibration_broadcaster_node; read it from there.
bool success
string message
float64 max_spread_deg
float64 mean_spread_deg
# Soft, informational confidence signal (2026-07-29) — true if the
# POST-outlier-rejection max_spread_deg/max position spread are both
# within position_spread_tolerance_cm/orientation_spread_tolerance_deg.
# Does NOT affect `success` above — a low-confidence result is still a
# real, broadcast, usable calibration; this field exists purely so a
# caller (web UI) can show a warning rather than silently trusting a
# result that may be less accurate than usual, without blocking the
# workflow on it.
bool is_high_confidence
---
# Feedback: published after each accepted sample.
uint32 samples_collected
uint32 samples_total
# Short, human-readable status text for the CURRENT event (2026-08-04) —
# e.g. "Sample 6 skipped: marker not found (no_yolo_bbox)" or
# "Waypoint 7: detect call timed out after 30.0s". Empty string for the
# normal "sample recorded successfully" feedback (samples_collected/
# samples_total already convey that case fully — this field exists
# specifically for the discard-and-continue/timeout events
# min_samples_to_finish's soft-fail path introduces, which previously had
# no user-visible signal at all outside calibration_broadcaster_node's own
# server-side log). Not cumulative/history — always just the latest event.
string current_status
# The just-recorded sample's known_chain_frame -> camera candidate pose
# (2026-07-29) — the SAME per-sample transform recordSample() already
# computes into collected_positions_/collected_orientations_ internally,
# now also surfaced here so a caller (web app, RViz via
# calibration_broadcaster_node's own transient per-sample TF broadcast) can
# visualize how the calibrated camera pose estimate is converging sample by
# sample, not just the final averaged result. Zero-valued (default Pose)
# on any feedback that isn't accompanied by a fresh sample (there are none
# today — every feedback publish in this node follows a recordSample()
# call — but this comment holds for any future caller relying on it).
geometry_msgs/Pose latest_sample_pose